	* `code`: Code representing the type of allergen (e.g., drug, food)
	* `severity`: Severity level of the reaction (e.g., mild, severe)
	* `onset`: Date and time when the reaction occurred or is expected to occur
2. **Map FHIR fields to HL7 v2 segments**:
	* `id` -> OBX-3: Observation Identifier (OID) [optional]
	* `patient` -> PID-1: Patient ID [required]
	* `code` -> OBX-4: Observation Code [required]
	* `severity` -> OBX-5: Observation Value [optional]
	* `onset` -> OBX-6: Observation Date/Time [optional]

Here's the JavaScript code that implements this mapping:
```javascript
function convertAllergyIntoleranceToFhirR4(allergyIntolerance) {
  const hl7v2Message = new HL7v2Message();

  // Map FHIR fields to HL7 v2 segments
  hl7v2Message.addSegment(new PIDSegment({
    patientId: allergyIntolerance.patient.reference,
  }));

  hl7v2Message.addSegment(new OBXSegment({
    observationIdentifier: allergyIntolerance.id, // optional
    observationCode: {
      codingSystem: 'http://snomed.org',
      code: allergyIntolerance.code.coding[0].code,
      display: allergyIntolerance.code.text,
    },
  }));

  if (allergyIntolerance.severity) {
    hl7v2Message.addSegment(new OBXSegment({
      observationValue: allergyIntolerance.severity,
    }));
  }

  if (allergyIntolerance.onset) {
    hl7v2Message.addSegment(new OBXSegment({
      observationDateTime: allergyIntolerance.onset,
    }));
  }

  return hl7v2Message;
}
