1. We first check if the `DocumentReference` has a valid identifier (`identifier.system`). If not, we throw an error.
2. Next, we verify that the document reference has a content type (`contentType`) that is supported by the Argonaut profile (`allowedContentTypes`). If not, we throw an error.
3. We then check if the document reference has a format (`format`) that is allowed by the Argonaut profile (`allowedFormats`). If not, we throw an error.
