* The `get`, `set`, and other special methods (e.g., `__contains__`, `__getitem__`, and `__setitem__`) provide an interface for interacting with the cache.
* When setting an item, if the cache exceeds its maximum size, it removes the least recently used item (LRU) by iterating over the keys in the dictionary and deleting the first one.

This implementation has O(1) complexity for most operations, including `get`, `set`, and checking if a key is present. The only operation with O(n) complexity is removing an LRU item when the cache exceeds its maximum size, which occurs at most once per cache insertion.

