Merging two arrays of equal size using the merge sort algorithm can be implemented in JavaScript as follows:

```javascript
function mergeSort(arr) {
  if (arr.length <= 1) return arr; // base case: single element or empty array

  const mid = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);
  const left = mergeSort(arr.slice(0, mid));
  const right = mergeSort(arr.slice(mid));

  return [...left, ...right].sort((a, b) => a - b); // merge the sorted halves
}
```

