Here's the step-by-step implementation:

**Class: `BFS`**

```java
import java.util.*;

public class BFS {
    // Queue for storing nodes at each level
    private Queue<Node> queue;

    // Array or hash set for storing visited nodes
    private boolean[] visited;

    public BFS(int size) {
        this.queue = new LinkedList<>();
        this.visited = new boolean[size];
    }

    public void bfs(Node startNode, int[][] graph) {
        // Initialize the queue with the starting node
        queue.add(startNode);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            Node current = queue.poll();

            // Visit all neighbors of the current node
            for (int i = 0; i < graph[current.id].length; i++) {
                if (!visited[graph[current.id][i]]) {
                    visited[graph[current.id][i]] = true;
                    queue.add(new Node(graph[current.id][i]));
                }
            }
        }
    }

    public class Node {
        int id;

        public Node(int id) {
            this.id = id;
        }
    }
}
```

**Usage:**

```java
int[][] graph = { /* your graph representation */ };
BFS bfs = new BFS(graph.length);

// Start the BFS from node 0 (or any other starting node)
bfs.bfs(new Node(0), graph);
```

